1
00:00:00,090 --> 00:00:03,569
Records administration starts
with finding the correct controls.

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:08,000
In the Records area, open All
records and choose Manage.

3
00:00:08,409 --> 00:00:11,470
The expanded menu contains
Settings and Definitions.

4
00:00:11,859 --> 00:00:16,090
Settings holds department-level
values; Definitions lets you inspect

5
00:00:16,090 --> 00:00:17,850
the forms and their own policies.

6
00:00:18,239 --> 00:00:19,370
Begin with Settings.

7
00:00:19,770 --> 00:00:23,670
This example uses the fictional
Firehouse fifty-one training department,

8
00:00:23,940 --> 00:00:26,979
so the practice changes stay with
a separate training environment.

9
00:00:27,229 --> 00:00:31,469
On Records Settings, Default lifecycle
preset for department definitions

10
00:00:31,469 --> 00:00:33,270
currently shows Quick Entry.

11
00:00:33,700 --> 00:00:36,410
Review due, in hours, is seventy-two.

12
00:00:36,970 --> 00:00:39,500
Record those baseline
values before practicing.

13
00:00:40,019 --> 00:00:44,099
The displayed help says locked
definitions retain their own lifecycle.

14
00:00:44,490 --> 00:00:48,659
It also says a definition-level
deadline override takes precedence

15
00:00:48,730 --> 00:00:50,159
over the department deadline.

16
00:00:50,640 --> 00:00:55,009
This is an administrative review interval;
the screen explicitly distinguishes

17
00:00:55,009 --> 00:00:56,640
it from a statutory deadline.

18
00:00:57,109 --> 00:01:00,780
Check the actual definition policy
as well as this department form

19
00:01:00,810 --> 00:01:02,440
when planning a review process.

20
00:01:02,619 --> 00:01:07,299
For this exercise, select Review
Required in Default lifecycle preset

21
00:01:07,299 --> 00:01:12,520
for department definitions, then enter
forty-eight in Review due, in hours.

22
00:01:12,860 --> 00:01:15,139
Both prepared values are visible together.

23
00:01:15,570 --> 00:01:18,879
Forty-eight hours is the training
example, not a recommended

24
00:01:18,879 --> 00:01:20,410
deadline for every department.

25
00:01:20,799 --> 00:01:24,010
Choose an interval that matches
your own review responsibilities.

26
00:01:24,449 --> 00:01:28,029
At this point the form is prepared
but has not yet been saved.

27
00:01:28,160 --> 00:01:30,390
Scroll to the bottom of Records Settings.

28
00:01:30,820 --> 00:01:34,179
Save and Cancel are visible below
the other settings sections.

29
00:01:34,560 --> 00:01:38,000
Review the intended change,
then choose Save once.

30
00:01:38,420 --> 00:01:41,430
Typing a value into a field
only prepares the form.

31
00:01:41,840 --> 00:01:44,940
The returned page and a fresh
page load give you a separate

32
00:01:44,940 --> 00:01:48,020
check that the intended values
were accepted and retained.

33
00:01:48,189 --> 00:01:51,310
The returned page displays
Records settings saved.

34
00:01:51,729 --> 00:01:56,930
The lifecycle field shows Review Required,
and the review deadline shows forty-eight.

35
00:01:57,449 --> 00:02:01,290
Compare both saved values with the
two values you intended to change.

36
00:02:01,639 --> 00:02:05,309
A success notice helps, and
inspecting the fields confirms which

37
00:02:05,309 --> 00:02:07,069
configuration is now displayed.

38
00:02:07,199 --> 00:02:11,509
Reopening Records Settings shows Review
Required and forty-eight hours again.

39
00:02:11,989 --> 00:02:14,330
This is a fresh page load after the save.

40
00:02:14,660 --> 00:02:17,809
It confirms that the department
form retained those values.

41
00:02:18,279 --> 00:02:21,649
The next check is the policy
on existing record definitions.

42
00:02:21,950 --> 00:02:25,890
A saved department value alone does
not tell you the lifecycle shown by

43
00:02:25,929 --> 00:02:27,929
every form that personnel can use.

44
00:02:28,130 --> 00:02:31,099
Return to All records
and expand Manage again.

45
00:02:31,599 --> 00:02:35,179
Choose Definitions from this
menu to inspect the record forms.

46
00:02:35,599 --> 00:02:38,790
This keeps the department settings
check separate from the definition

47
00:02:38,790 --> 00:02:42,689
check, while giving administrators
a repeatable route to both screens.

48
00:02:42,799 --> 00:02:46,480
The Definitions table includes
Owner, Published version and

49
00:02:46,480 --> 00:02:48,060
Lifecycle preset columns.

50
00:02:48,530 --> 00:02:51,390
Run and Training are
marked Product, locked.

51
00:02:51,770 --> 00:02:54,529
Both show published version
one and Quick Entry.

52
00:02:54,930 --> 00:02:57,430
This screen was captured while
the department form had the

53
00:02:57,430 --> 00:02:59,539
saved Review Required value.

54
00:02:59,949 --> 00:03:04,289
The locked definitions still show their
own Quick Entry policy, matching the scope

55
00:03:04,289 --> 00:03:06,140
described in the department settings help.

56
00:03:06,619 --> 00:03:09,080
Read the row you actually intend to use.

57
00:03:09,270 --> 00:03:13,919
In the same table, locate Training
Only, Community software exercise.

58
00:03:14,330 --> 00:03:18,399
Its owner is Department, and its
lifecycle column shows Quick Entry.

59
00:03:18,800 --> 00:03:20,340
The row has an Edit link.

60
00:03:20,750 --> 00:03:23,380
Choose Edit to inspect
that definition version.

61
00:03:23,880 --> 00:03:28,179
Use the definition name and owner to
distinguish a department-owned form from

62
00:03:28,179 --> 00:03:32,189
a locked product form before deciding
which policy you are maintaining.

63
00:03:32,379 --> 00:03:35,750
The definition page identifies
version one as Published.

64
00:03:36,119 --> 00:03:40,280
Its notice says this version is
published and read-only, and it

65
00:03:40,280 --> 00:03:42,729
offers Open new draft for changes.

66
00:03:43,080 --> 00:03:47,719
Lifecycle preset still shows Quick Entry
on this existing published definition.

67
00:03:48,130 --> 00:03:51,289
Review the version you are
inspecting before planning an edit.

68
00:03:51,699 --> 00:03:56,369
This walkthrough reads the existing
policy; it leaves Open new draft available

69
00:03:56,369 --> 00:03:58,830
for a separate definition-change exercise.

70
00:03:59,030 --> 00:04:03,220
Farther down the same definition
page are Reviewer roles, Approver

71
00:04:03,220 --> 00:04:05,999
roles and Review due, in hours.

72
00:04:06,320 --> 00:04:09,020
The review deadline field
is blank in this example.

73
00:04:09,449 --> 00:04:12,890
These are definition-specific
controls to inspect when deciding

74
00:04:12,890 --> 00:04:14,609
how that form should be reviewed.

75
00:04:15,039 --> 00:04:17,980
The department settings help
explains the precedence of a

76
00:04:17,980 --> 00:04:20,060
definition-level deadline override.

77
00:04:20,400 --> 00:04:23,970
Keep role assignments, the
selected lifecycle and the review

78
00:04:23,970 --> 00:04:27,390
interval consistent with the
people responsible for the process.

79
00:04:27,689 --> 00:04:30,359
This inspection does not
change the published version.

80
00:04:30,560 --> 00:04:33,280
Return to Records Settings
after the exercise.

81
00:04:33,740 --> 00:04:37,579
The prepared restoration selects
Quick Entry and enters seventy-two

82
00:04:37,619 --> 00:04:39,249
hours, matching the baseline.

83
00:04:39,679 --> 00:04:42,889
Compare both fields with the
values you recorded at the start.

84
00:04:43,440 --> 00:04:46,689
Restoring a practice change should
be an intentional configuration

85
00:04:46,689 --> 00:04:51,230
decision, using the same review of the
complete form as the original change.

86
00:04:51,360 --> 00:04:54,209
Use the same Save action at
the bottom of the settings

87
00:04:54,209 --> 00:04:55,910
form to apply the restoration.

88
00:04:56,410 --> 00:04:59,920
The original values are still
only prepared until you save them.

89
00:05:00,339 --> 00:05:03,460
Verify the returned result
before ending the exercise.

90
00:05:03,659 --> 00:05:05,619
Records settings saved appears again.

91
00:05:06,040 --> 00:05:10,100
Quick Entry and seventy-two hours are
now displayed on the returned form.

92
00:05:10,520 --> 00:05:13,919
The demonstration has restored
its original department defaults.

93
00:05:14,280 --> 00:05:18,490
No record was submitted for review,
and no definition version was edited or

94
00:05:18,490 --> 00:05:20,729
published during this settings exercise.

95
00:05:20,909 --> 00:05:25,110
A final reopening still shows
Quick Entry and seventy-two hours.

96
00:05:25,660 --> 00:05:29,930
Use this same baseline, save,
reopen and definition-inspection

97
00:05:29,930 --> 00:05:31,369
process for your department.

98
00:05:31,850 --> 00:05:36,669
Security teams can organize post-report
review, wildland contractors can review

99
00:05:36,699 --> 00:05:41,349
crew-support records, and industrial teams
can coordinate exercise documentation.

100
00:05:41,859 --> 00:05:45,480
Community paramedicine and mental
health teams can define appropriate

101
00:05:45,519 --> 00:05:48,990
outreach review responsibilities,
while search-and-rescue teams can

102
00:05:48,990 --> 00:05:51,009
review mission-support documentation.

103
00:05:51,519 --> 00:05:54,510
Fire and E M S departments
can use the same checks.

104
00:05:54,940 --> 00:05:59,519
Set a clear policy, then verify the
specific form personnel will use.
